[{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>In each case, choose one of the statements</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A\\Rightarrow B\\qquad A\\Leftarrow B\\qquad A\\Leftrightarrow B\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>to describe the relationship between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: The shape has 4 equal sides.<br><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: The shape is a square.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: A quadrilateral has perpendicular diagonals.<br><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: The quadrilateral is a kite.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: A quadrilateral has one pair of parallel sides.<br><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: The quadrilateral is a trapezium.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"PQRS\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a rhombus.<br><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"PQRS\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a parallelogram.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\Leftarrow B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\Leftarrow B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\Leftrightarrow B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\Rightarrow B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>In each case, choose one of the statements</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A\\Rightarrow B\\qquad A\\Leftarrow B\\qquad A\\Leftrightarrow B\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>to describe the relationship between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x-3)(x+2)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\Rightarrow B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\Leftarrow B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\Rightarrow B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\\Leftrightarrow B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>For each of the following determine which of these statements are true, where it is false explain your answer:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an even integer, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even</p></li><li><p>The product of 5 consecutive integers is a multiple of 5</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\in\\mathbb R\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>The square root of a positive number is always positive</p></li><li><p>The product of any two odd integers is always even</p></li><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos x{}^\\circ=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=60\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>True</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>True</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>False, not true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>True</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>False. It is always odd.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p>False as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> could be another value such as 300 for example</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Find the mistake in the proof below:</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2=\\frac{20}{10}=\\frac{10+10}{10}=\\frac{(10-10)(10+10)}{10(10-10)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=\\frac{10^2-10^2}{100-100}=\\frac{100-100}{100-100}=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>At the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{(10-10)(10+10)}{10(10-10)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> there is a zero in the denominator</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>For each statement, find an example that disproves it:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>All prime numbers are odd.</p></li><li><p>All squares are even numbers.</p></li><li><p>All multiples of 3 are also multiples of 6</p></li><li><p>All real numbers have a square root.</p></li><li><p>All perfect squares end in an odd number.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>2 is a prime number and its even.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^2=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is odd.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>3 is a multiple of 3 but not a multiple of 6</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> does not have a real square root.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4=2^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> ends in an even number.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>For each statement, find an example that disproves it:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^4&gt;x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a prime number, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^2-n+13\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is prime.</p></li><li><p>The value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^2+n+17\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a prime number for all positive integer values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^4=(-2)^4=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16&gt;-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2\\not&gt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> not true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"13^2-13+13=13^2=169\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is not a prime number.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16^2+16+17=16(16+1)+17=17^2=289\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is not a prime number.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Use proof by exhaustion to prove that</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the sum of the digits of any 2-digit number is less than or equal to 18</p></li><li><p>if a 2-digit number is divisible by 3, then the sum of its digits is divisible by 3</p></li><li><p>89 is a prime number.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Combinations to form a 2 digit number:</p>","<div class=\"math-table\"><table><tr><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"+\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p>0</p></td><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>11</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>12</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>13</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>13</p></td><td><p>14</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>13</p></td><td><p>14</p></td><td><p>15</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>13</p></td><td><p>14</p></td><td><p>15</p></td><td><p>16</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>13</p></td><td><p>14</p></td><td><p>15</p></td><td><p>16</p></td><td><p>17</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>13</p></td><td><p>14</p></td><td><p>15</p></td><td><p>16</p></td><td><p>17</p></td><td><p>18</p></td></tr></table></div>","<p>Therefore, the sum of the digits of any 2-digit number is less than or equal to 18</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Combinations to form a 2 digit number, which are divisible by 3:</p>","<div class=\"math-table\"><table><tr><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"+\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p>0</p></td><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>3</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>6</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td></td><td><p>3</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>6</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>6</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>12</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>6</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>12</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td></td><td><p>6</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>12</p></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>12</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>15</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>12</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>15</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>8</p></td><td></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>12</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>15</p></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>12</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>15</p></td><td></td><td></td><td><p>18</p></td></tr></table></div>","<p>Therefore if a 2-digit number is divisible by 3, then the sum of its digits is divisible by 3</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{89}=9.43\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so check prime numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"&lt;9.43\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"89\\div7=12.71\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"89\\div5=17.8\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"89\\div3=29.66\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"89\\div2=4.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>None of these are integers, so 89 is a prime number.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Prove that no square number ends in a 3</p>","steps":["<p>Consider the end digits of every number</p>","<div class=\"math-table\"><table><tr><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"+\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p>0</p></td><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>9</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\wedge2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p>0</p></td><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>1</p></td></tr></table></div>","<p>None of these have 3 as the final digit, so we have proved the original statement that no square number ends in a 3</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Show that</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the sum of 2 consecutive numbers is always odd.</p></li><li><p>the sum of any two consecutive odd numbers is a multiple of 4</p></li><li><p>the square of an odd number is always odd.</p></li><li><p>the sum of the squares of 2 consecutive odd numbers is always even.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Two consecutive numbers: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2k)+(2k+1)=4k+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> the sum of 2 consecutive numbers is always odd</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Two consecutive numbers: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2k+1)+(2k+3)=4k+4=4(k+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> the sum of any two consecutive odd numbers is a multiple of 4</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Odd number: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2k+1)^2=4k^2+4k+1=2(2k^2+2k)+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> The square of an odd number is always odd.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Two consecutive odd numbers: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n (2k+1)^2+(2k+3)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =4k^2+4k+1+4k^2+12k+9\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =8k^2+16k+10\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =2(4k^2+8k+5)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> The sum of the squares of 2 consecutive odd numbers is always even.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Prove</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the product of any three consecutive positive integers is a multiple of 6</p></li><li><p>the product of any four consecutive positive integers is a multiple of 24</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Three consecutive positive integers:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k,k+1,k+2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At least one of these is even so divisible by 2</p>","<p>One of these must be a multiple of 3</p>","<p>As the expression is a multiple of both 2 and 3, it must be a multiple of 6</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Four consecutive positive integers:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k,k+1,k+2,k+3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At least two of these are even:</p>","<p>One must be divisible by 2 the other by 4</p>","<p>One of these must be a multiple of 3</p>","<p>As the expression is a multiple of both 2, 3 and 4, it must be a multiple of 24</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Prove that for any even number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the expression <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6n^2+10n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a factor of 4</p>","steps":["<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=2k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n6n^2+10n =6(2k)^2+10(2k)=24k^2+20k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =4(6k^2+5k)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore 6n^2+10n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a factor of 4</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^4-n^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 6 for all positive integer values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nn^4-n^2 =n^2(n^2-1)=n^2(n-1)(n+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =n\\times[(n-1)\\times n\\times(n+1)]\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So it is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> the product of three consecutive integers.</p>","<p>Three consecutive positive integers:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"n-1,n,n+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At least one of these is even so divisible by 2</p>","<p>One of these must be a multiple of 3</p>","<p>As the expression is a multiple of both 2 and 3, it must be a multiple of 6</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>Prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^3-n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 3 for all positive integer values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, using</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Proof by deduction</p></li><li><p>Proof by cases, by considering <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=3k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=3k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=3k+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"n^3-n=n(n^2-1)=n(n-1)(n+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So it is three consecutive numbers positive integers: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n-1,n,n+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>One of these must be a multiple of 3</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^3-n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be a multiple of 3</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"n^3-n=n(n^2-1)=n(n-1)(n+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=3m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3m)^3-(3m)=3m(3m-1)(3m+1)\\text{ which is divisible by 3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=3m+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n (3m+1)^3-(3m+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(3m+1)(3m+1-1)(3m+1+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(3m+1)3m(3m+2)\\text{ which is divisible by 3}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=3m+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n (3m+2)^3-(3m+2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(3m+2)(3m+2-1)(3m+2+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(3m+2)(3m+1)(3m+3)\\text{which is divisible by 3}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^3-n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be a multiple of 3</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.45-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>For a positive integer number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^4-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not divisible by 8</p>","steps":["<p>Consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is even: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=2k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"n^4-4=(2k)^4-4=16k^4-4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>This is 4 less than a multiple of 8, hence not divisible by 8</p>","<p>Consider <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=2k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nn^4-4 =(2k+1)^4-4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =16k^4+32k^3+24k^2+8k+1-4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =8(2k^4+4k^3+3k^2+k)-3\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>This is 3 less than a multiple of 8, hence not divisible by 8</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore n^4-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not divisible by 8</p>"]}]